llamafile sgemm: Q5_0 x Q8_0 on arm64 through tinyBLAS_Q0_ARM

Q5_0 had a tinyBLAS path for AVX only, and neither KleidiAI nor the repack code takes Q5_0, so on arm64 every Q5_0
matmul ran the generic per-element ggml_vec_dot_q5_0_q8_0 (about 60 instructions per 64 MACs, scratchpad bughunt asm).
Ling-3.0-tiny stores its shared experts (ffn_*_shexp, 12 layers) in Q5_0. This adds load_lo/load_hi that expand the
5th bit from qh with vtst and uses the existing dotprod tile code. ggml-cpu.c undefines GGML_USE_LLAMAFILE on every
i8mm or SVE build, so it also keeps llamafile for Q5_0 matmuls there (prefill only: llamafile needs n >= 2).
Numerics: the int8 values and integer dot products are the same as the generic path. Under QEMU (arm64), each
tinyBLAS output matched ggml_vec_dot_q5_0_q8_0 within 1.2e-7 (outputs up to 1.8). Ling's logits still moved: KL
against stock mean 0.002, max 0.011, same top token 98.4%, perplexity 11.122 -> 11.085 (256 tokens). Likely
cause (not proven): the rounding-level change flips near-tied expert choices in the 8-of-128 MoE routing. Needs the
eval. Phone speed: not measured yet.

